= Mass =

#type: node
#context: sop
#internal: a3ob_mass
#tags: arma, p3d

"""Sets the mass of each point of a Geometry LOD (the #Mass# data of the P3D file)."""

Arma needs a mass for each point of a Geometry LOD to work out how a vehicle or object moves. This node sets that mass in one of several ways.

@inputs

LOD geometry:
    Input 1.

@parameters

Mode:
    #id: mode

    What to do with the mass.

    Type: Menu. Default: Uniform total.

    Set on each:
        Sets this to Set on each.

    Uniform total:
        Sets this to Uniform total.

    From density:
        Sets this to From density.

    Clear:
        Sets this to Clear.

    Copy from mass:
        Sets this to Copy from mass.

    Copy to mass:
        Sets this to Copy to mass.

Value:
    #id: value

    Set on each: kilograms per point. Uniform total: kilograms shared by all the points. From density: kilograms per cubic metre. The value cannot be below 0; there is no upper limit (the slider shows 0 to 10, and you can type more).

    Type: Number. Default: 1. Allowed: At least 0; no upper limit.

Group:
    #id: group

    The points to change. Empty means all points.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Visualize:
    #id: visualize

    Write the colour Cd: blue is the least mass, red the most, black no mass. The export ignores Cd.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

The full page for this node is docs/user/reference/a3ob_mass.html in the A3OB folder. Open it in a web browser.
